cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline in academic work, please cite it as below."

title: "DIW Bioprinting -- Portable Analysis Pipeline"

abstract: >-
  Self-contained Python + MATLAB tooling for characterising
  direct ink writing (DIW) bioinks: fitting rheological constitutive
  models (Power Law, Cross, Carreau, Herschel-Bulkley, Bingham,
  Casson, Ellis) to flow-curve data, extracting SAOS / recovery /
  h_max parameters from oscillatory rheology, simulating
  syringe-needle extrusion (Power-Law and Cross solvers, straight or
  tapered geometries) to produce slicer-lookup tables, and
  validating prints from images via the Ouyang printability index.

type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-05-21

